    "created_at": "2016-05-11T05:59:58Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-05-11T06:18:15Z",
    "body": "Just follow up:\n\nI'm thinking about following scenario:\n\n```\n// Provided third-party\nclass X extends HTMLElement { ... }\nwindow.customElements.define('my-x', X);\n\n// I want to more feature to X\nclass Y extends  X { ... }\n\n// Then install my tag\nwindow.customElements.define('my-y', Y);\n```\n\nIn this case, I don't need to register \"my-x\" tag name, third party library should split element registration and class implementation.\n\nIn this case, Y is in custom element registration table and (new Y()).constructor == Y.\n",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
